# CI workflow (reference)

Copy this file to `.github/workflows/ci.yml` to enable CI.

> Note: the development sandbox's GitHub App does not have the `workflows`
> permission, so workflow files cannot be pushed from there. The project
> owner can add this file directly, or grant the app the "workflows"
> permission (Repository settings → Permissions → Workflows).

```yaml
name: CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [main, "arena/**"]
  pull_request:

jobs:
  core-tests:
    name: Core unit tests (JVM)
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Set up JDK 17
        uses: actions/setup-java@v4
        with:
          distribution: temurin
          java-version: "17"

      - name: Make Gradle executable
        run: chmod +x gradlew

      - name: Run core tests
        run: ./gradlew :core:test --no-daemon

      - name: Build core module
        run: ./gradlew :core:build --no-daemon
```
